

1. Agreement
---

The Lender, Chadwick Lending Inc., and the Borrower, Anthony Enterprises Inc., hereby agree to the terms and conditions of this Loan Agreement, executed on the 1st day of July, 1991, in West Courtney, Somalia. This Agreement is entered into for the purpose of funding the Borrower's operations. The parties agree to the following terms:

2. Recitals
---

2. Recitals

A. Borrower Requirements

The Borrower, Anthony Enterprises Inc., is in need of capital to fund its operations.

B. Lender's Willingness

Chadwick Lending Inc., as the Lender, is willing to provide such capital to the Borrower.

C. Agreement

In light of the foregoing, the parties have agreed to enter into this Loan Agreement on the Agreement Date, with the intention that the Lender will lend funds to the Borrower, and the Borrower will repay the loan amount in accordance with the terms and conditions set forth herein.

3. Definitions
---

The following terms, as used in this Agreement, shall have the meanings set forth below:

3.1 "Lender" shall mean Chadwick Lending Inc., a corporation organized and existing under the laws of the State of Delaware, with its principal place of business at 46455 Margaret View Suite 329, Christopherberg, RI 78460, and having its email address at chadwilson@example.net and its telephone number at (001) 815-743-0872x9395.

3.2 "Borrower" shall mean Anthony Enterprises Inc., a corporation organized and existing under the laws of the State of New York, with its principal place of business at 663 David Meadows, Port Anthony, KS 39368, and having its email address at uoliver@example.com and its telephone number at (614) 525-0934x63273.

3.3 "Agreement" shall mean this Loan Agreement dated July 1, 1991, between the Lender and the Borrower.

3.4 "Jurisdiction" shall mean West Courtney, Somalia.

3.5 "Loan Purpose" shall mean the funding of the Borrower's operations.

3.6 "Interest Rate" shall mean an annual interest rate of 11%.

3.7 "Repayment Terms" shall mean the Borrower's agreement to repay the loan amount in 5 years.

4. Loan
---

The Lender agrees to make a loan to the Borrower in the amount necessary to fund the Borrower's operations as of the Agreement Date, with the principal and interest to be repaid in accordance with the Repayment Terms. The Loan shall bear interest at a rate of 11% per annum, calculated on the basis of a 360-day year, and payable semi-annually in arrears. The Borrower shall make the first payment on the anniversary of the Agreement Date.

5. Interest
---

5. Interest

The Borrower agrees to pay interest on the loan amount at a rate of eleven percent (11%) per annum. The interest shall be calculated on a daily basis and shall be compounded annually. The Borrower shall pay the interest along with the principal amount on the due dates specified in Section 6 (Repayment).

6. Repayment
---

The Borrower, Anthony Enterprises Inc., agrees to repay the loan amount extended by Chadwick Lending Inc., together with interest at the rate of 11%, within a period of five (5) years from the Agreement Date of July 1, 1991, in West Courtney, Somalia. The repayment schedule shall be mutually agreed upon by the Parties. Any delay or failure to make timely repayment shall constitute a default under this Agreement.

7. Security
---

The Borrower grants to the Lender a security interest in all of its present and future assets, whether now owned or hereafter acquired, to secure the loan made hereunder. The Borrower agrees to execute and deliver such further instruments and to take such further action as the Lender may reasonably request to perfect, maintain, and enforce the security interest granted hereunder.

In the event of the Borrower's default under this Agreement, the Lender shall have the right to sell, assign, transfer, or otherwise dispose of the collateral securing the loan, without further notice to the Borrower, and to apply the proceeds of such sale towards the payment of the outstanding loan amount, including accrued interest, costs, and expenses. The Borrower shall be responsible for paying any deficiency remaining after the application of the proceeds of such sale.

The Borrower acknowledges and agrees that the security interest granted hereunder is a continuing security interest, and it shall continue in effect until the loan and all amounts owing under this Agreement have been fully repaid. The Borrower further agrees that the Lender may, from time to time, require the Borrower to furnish additional collateral to secure the loan, and the Borrower shall comply with such request promptly.

The Borrower shall keep the Lender informed of the location and condition of the collateral securing the loan, and the Borrower shall permit the Lender, at any time, to inspect and examine the collateral and the books and records of the Borrower relating to the collateral. The Borrower shall also deliver to the Lender such additional documents and information as the Lender may reasonably request to perfect, maintain, and enforce the security interest granted hereunder.

In the event of any conflict between the provisions of this Agreement and the provisions of any other agreement between the Parties, the provisions of this Agreement shall control with respect to the security interest granted hereunder.

The Borrower hereby waives any right it may have under applicable law to exempt the collateral securing the loan from the Lender's claims and remedies with respect to the loan. The Borrower further agrees that the Lender may, at any time, without notice to the Borrower, take possession of the collateral securing the loan and sell, assign, transfer, or otherwise dispose of the collateral to satisfy the loan and any amounts owing under this Agreement.

The Borrower shall not, without the prior written consent of the Lender, encumber, pledge, or otherwise dispose of any of the collateral securing the loan, or permit any lien or encumbrance to be placed upon any of the collateral, except as permitted by this Agreement. Any such encumbrance or disposition made in violation of this provision shall be void and unenforceable.

8. Covenants
---

The Borrower, Anthony Enterprises Inc., covenants and agrees that:

8.1. It shall use the Loan proceeds solely for the purpose of funding its operations.

8.2. It shall promptly notify the Lender of any material changes in its financial condition or business operations.

8.3. It shall maintain accurate and complete financial records and make them available to the Lender upon request.

8.4. It shall not, without the prior written consent of the Lender, incur any additional indebtedness or liens, create any security interests, or pledge any of its assets.

8.5. It shall comply with all applicable laws, regulations, and ordinances in the conduct of its business.

8.6. It shall keep the Lender informed of its financial condition and provide periodic financial statements.

8.7. It shall not, without the prior written consent of the Lender, assign, transfer, or encumber any of its rights or obligations under this Agreement.

8.8. It shall cooperate fully with the Lender in connection with any audit or review of its financial statements or operations.

8.9. It shall pay all taxes, assessments, and other governmental charges that may be levied upon it, and shall keep all property of the Lender free and clear of any liens, encumbrances, or other claims.

8.10. It shall perform all other acts and do all other things necessary or desirable to carry out the purposes of this Agreement.

These covenants shall survive the repayment of the Loan.

9. Default
---

In the event that the Borrower fails to make any payment when due or otherwise breaches any of its covenants under this Agreement, the Lender shall have the right to declare all amounts owing under this Agreement immediately due and payable. Upon such declaration, the Borrower shall pay to the Lender interest on any unpaid amount at the rate of 11% per annum, from the date such amount became due until paid in full. The Lender may also, without limiting any other rights or remedies available to it, exercise any rights of set-off, counterclaim, recoupment, marshalling of assets or other legal or equitable remedies available to it under the laws of West Courtney, Somalia. The Borrower shall indemnify and hold harmless the Lender from and against any loss, damage, cost or expense (including reasonable attorneys' fees) incurred by the Lender as a result of such default.

10. Indemnification
---

10. Indemnification

    10.1 Lender shall indemnify, defend and hold harmless Borrower, its officers, directors, employees, agents and affiliates from and against any and all losses, liabilities, damages, costs, expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of or in connection with any claim, action, suit, or proceeding brought against Borrower by reason of any breach or alleged breach by Lender of any representation, warranty, covenant or agreement made by Lender in this Agreement.

    10.2 Borrower shall indemnify, defend and hold harmless Lender, its officers, directors, employees, agents and affiliates from and against any and all losses, liabilities, damages, costs, expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of or in connection with any claim, action, suit, or proceeding brought against Lender by reason of any breach or alleged breach by Borrower of any representation, warranty, covenant or agreement made by Borrower in this Agreement.

    10.3 The indemnification provided in this Section shall survive the termination or expiration of this Agreement.

    10.4 Each indemnified party shall promptly notify the indemnifying party in writing of any claim, action, suit or proceeding of which it becomes aware, and shall allow the indemnifying party the right to assume the defense of such claim, action, suit or proceeding with counsel of its own choosing. The indemnified party shall cooperate fully with the indemnifying party in the defense of such claim, action, suit or proceeding.

    10.5 The indemnifying party shall not be liable for any settlement of any claim, action, suit or proceeding effected without its written consent, which shall not be unreasonably withheld or delayed.

    10.6 The indemnifying party shall have the right to participate in the defense of any claim, action, suit or proceeding.

    10.7 The indemnification provided in this Section shall be in addition to, and not in lieu of, any other rights or remedies to which the indemnifying party may be entitled.

    10.8 This Section shall be binding upon and inure to the benefit of the respective successors and assigns of the Parties.

11. Governing Law
---

This Loan Agreement shall be governed by the laws of West Courtney, Somalia.

